host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title Caravan appeal -- the reader who is told how a quarrel came out may answer that telling
prompt Keaton asked for the next agent-doable lap, Lindy-first crux-first, on the running thread the last log's recommend named.
think The running thread is the Caravan correction arc, sixty-seven rungs deep. The tidings log's recommend named the crux exactly: nothing in this arc lets the person who was told the word stood answer that telling, and an answer with no way to answer it back is a door that only opens outward.
think Standfast first. Every row in crux/REDS.md reads CLOSED, %96 and %97 among them, so no red preempts constructive work this lap.
think The rung is appeal. Its measurement is readers who answered how their quarrel came out and whom no run ever read -- the first number of this arc that weighs what a reader reached back rather than what the run reached outward.
think The act is two halves facing opposite ways. The reader writes one byte into their own caravan/.readers/desk.press -- a for an outcome they accept, p for a quarrel they press still. The run reads it and writes one byte into caravan/.appeals/plan.appeal, where an operator opens the plan.
think A plea is quoted and never composed. press_as_reader carries the same restraint answer_as_reader and renew_as_reader carry: no run of this plan ever calls it, because a supervisor that could file a plea on a reader's behalf would be pressing an objection it invented and then reading its own handwriting back as consent.
think The build is a delegating layer, as every rung of this arc is. The tidings layer became a delegation block, the report accessors each deepened one tier, and the new layer added its enum, its byte, its two counts, its four refusals, and its one measurement.
think The lap is one plan run twice under the same tidings word, parted only by the appeal word, and a third run that proves the accepting plea beside the renewing reader already proven below.
obs A plea reports where a person stands and settles nothing. The rung reopens no quarrel, reverses no settlement, and grades no objection -- it records that the person who raised it is content or is not, which is the one thing the record could never say before.
obs The five RED paths were proven on metal before the claim. Publish the other plea and the run refuses AppealMisrecorded. Count one reader twice and it refuses AppealMiscounted. File a plea the reader never wrote and it refuses AppealUnvoiced.
obs An honest intermediate finding, and the same one the repose rung reported: reaching AppealEarly on the wire took disarming the count invariant and the closed-run invariant first, because both fire before the refusal can. The asserts are doing their job; the refusal is the door behind them.
obs The planted control is the one worth naming. With the note never written, the read-back skipped, the provisioning invariant removed, and all three harness reads that catch them gone, the selftest printed GREEN while caravan/.appeals/plan.appeal still held the cleared zero byte the provisioning wrote -- an operator opening the plan reading nothing at all -- beside a desk.press reading a that nobody ever opened. Seeing that once is what makes the reading back a check rather than decoration.
obs The touch opened a 70-line ratchet in the telling, so it split at its own seam: everything the rungs below report stands in tell_appeal_runs, and the reading back the two plans actually disagree about stands in tell_appeal_half.
obs Registered in the choir the same round, per REDS %81's lesson -- a rung that lands as its own green witness and never joins the suite is a loom firing unheard. caravan/.appeals joined the ignore roster beside its siblings.
obs The council rota doc this lap was item 14, Radiant Style with Twilight beside it, taken as choir count 68 mod 27. Its pendulum -- aim, then dissolve -- shaped the header prose: each claim named plainly, then opened outward.
loom witness=caravan_appeal_witness result=GREEN rungs_sung=68 phases=6 dependents=6 absorbed=3 lost=3 reseated=3 heard_back=1 unread_closed=1 unread_open=0
file caravan/appeal.rye the rung itself -- the appeal layer over the tidings rung, delegating whole and adding one reading back
file tools/caravan_appeal_witness.rish the witness on metal -- the fold, both pleas on the wire, the three-run lap, and every note read outside the run that wrote it
file tools/caravan_suite_witness.rish registers the new rung so the choir sings 68 in one voice
file caravan/README.md the durable record of the rung, in the arc's own table and its own section
file .gitignore caravan/.appeals joins the ignore roster beside its siblings
file crux/REMEMBER.md the live card names this edge and folds the one below it to a pointer
recommend keep-going the arc now corrects a record, carries the correction where it is read, hears the answer, records the disagreement, escorts the word, bounds the objection, stands its standing in the mark, tells the raiser how it came out, and reads what they say back -- so the question above it is what a run owes a reader whose plea says the quarrel is not over: the record holds their pressing and every note of it is one run deep, which means a plan run again tomorrow starts from a person whose position it has already forgotten.
